Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
8 x + 6+\left(4 y + 2\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(4 y + 2\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(8 x + 6\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{8 x + 6}{4 y + 2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{-18}{-14}=- \frac{9}{7}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=- \frac{9}{7}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(-4\right)&=- \frac{9}{7}\left(x-\left(-3\right)\right) \\
y&=- \frac{9}{7}\left(x-\left(-3\right)\right)+\left(-4\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
0&=- \frac{9}{7}\left(x-\left(-3\right)\right)+\left(-4\right) \\
x-\left(-3\right)&=-\frac{-4}{- \frac{9}{7}} \\
x&=- \frac{55}{9}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(- \frac{55}{9},0\right)$.

Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
2 x + 4+\left(-4\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(-4\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(2 x + 4\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{2 x + 4}{-4}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{10}{-4}=\frac{5}{2}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=\frac{5}{2}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(-1\right)&=\frac{5}{2}\left(x-\left(3\right)\right) \\
y&=\frac{5}{2}\left(x-\left(3\right)\right)+\left(-1\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y&=\frac{5}{2}\left(0-\left(3\right)\right)+\left(-1\right) \\
y&=- \frac{17}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(0,- \frac{17}{2}\right)$.

Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:

$$
\begin{aligned}
2 x+\left(8 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\
\left(8 y\right)\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\left(2 x\right) \\
\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{2 x}{8 y}
\end{aligned}
$$

Evaluate the tangent slope at the given point:

$$
m_{\mathrm{t}}=-\frac{4}{-32}=\frac{1}{8}
$$

The tangent line uses $m=\frac{1}{8}$.

Use the given point and this slope:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y-\left(-4\right)&=\frac{1}{8}\left(x-\left(2\right)\right) \\
y&=\frac{1}{8}\left(x-\left(2\right)\right)+\left(-4\right)
\end{aligned}
$$

At the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:

$$
\begin{aligned}
y&=\frac{1}{8}\left(0-\left(2\right)\right)+\left(-4\right) \\
y&=- \frac{17}{4}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore $P=\left(0,- \frac{17}{4}\right)$.
